  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Russia-Ukraine talks ‘very productive,’ says US’s Rubio – as it happened",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/nov/10/ukraine-russia-war-us-talks-abu-dhabi-europe-latest-news-updates",
      "description": "<p>US-led talks in Abu Dhabi break up after four hours but are expected to resume tomorrow as Zelenskyy says humanitarian issues were discussed</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/10/us-officials-russia-ukraine-war-abu-dhabi-talks\">US officials seek ‘final end’ to Russia-Ukraine war as talks begin</a></p></li></ul><p>The EU has said it stands ready “to come with a swift and united response” after France blamed Iran for a spate of cyber-attacks on supermarket freezers and chillers that caused millions of euros of damage.</p><p>Speaking to journalists on Monday, French foreign minister <strong>Jean-Noël Barrot</strong> said “<strong>Europe-wide sanctions</strong>” would be imposed against those responsible as he announced <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/09/france-blames-irans-revolutionary-guards-for-cyber-attacks-on-supermarket-fridges\">France believed that Iran’s Revolutionary Guards were “responsible for this attack”</a>.</p><p><em>We acknowledge that France has attributed these (cyber-attacks) to Iran. Pending discussions with member states, we as (the) European Union, <strong>we stand ready to come with a swift and united response</strong>.</em></p><p><em>We as the EU, <strong>we have consistently called on all states to refrain from malicious behaviour in the cyberspace</strong>. And we will continue to address such malicious behavior, making use of all the tools that we have also under the EU cyber diplomacy toolbox, including sanctions.</em></p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/nov/10/ukraine-russia-war-us-talks-abu-dhabi-europe-latest-news-updates\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-10T17:05:05"
    },
    {
      "title": "US officials seek ‘final end’ to Russia-Ukraine war, as Abu Dhabi talks set to continue",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/10/us-officials-russia-ukraine-war-abu-dhabi-talks",
      "description": "<p>First substantive peace talks since February include US proposal for ‘long-term security architecture’ between Moscow and Europe</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/nov/10/ukraine-russia-war-us-talks-abu-dhabi-europe-latest-news-updates\">Europe live – latest updates</a></p></li></ul><p>US officials have said they are seeking a “final end” to the war between Russia and Ukraine as trilateral talks got under way in Abu Dhabi, the first substantive negotiations between the two countries since February.</p><p>The talks, which are set to go into a planned second day on Wednesday, are also the first since the US launched joint strikes with Israel against Iran, and they follow bruising midterm elections that have weakened Donald Trump at home.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/10/us-officials-russia-ukraine-war-abu-dhabi-talks\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-10T16:59:04"
    },
    {
      "title": "Russia and Ukraine begin U.S.-backed peace talks in Abu Dhabi",
      "link": "https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/2026/11/10/russia-ukraine-begin-us-backed-peace-talks-abu-dhabi/",
      "description": "The talks are expected to include a broad discussion of European security, a move observers described as a risky nod to a key Russian goal of having a greater say in Europe’s security.",
      "source_name": "Washington Post World",
      "published": "2026-11-10T18:40:33"
    }
  ]
